<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>Lauren Cho's Portfolio</title>
  <style>
    :root {
      --desktop-pink: #f7bfd2; --desktop-pink-dark: #e993b5;
      --mac-gray: #d8d8d8; --mac-gray-light: #f3f3f3;
      --mac-gray-mid: #b9b9b9; --mac-gray-dark: #777777;
      --mac-black: #111111; --mac-white: #ffffff;
      --pink-soft: #ffe7f0; --pink-card: #fff4f8;
      --pink-hot: #d84f8b; --text: #151515;
    }
    * { box-sizing: border-box; }
    html, body {
      margin: 0; min-height: 100%;
      font-family: "Chicago", "Geneva", "Monaco", "Courier New", monospace;
      background:
        radial-gradient(circle at 20px 20px, rgba(255,255,255,0.38) 0 2px, transparent 3px),
        linear-gradient(135deg, var(--desktop-pink), #ffd9e7 45%, #f5a8c6);
      background-size: 26px 26px, 100% 100%;
      color: var(--text);
    }
    body { padding: 18px; }
    .system-menu {
      position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 10;
      width: min(1200px, 100%); margin: 0 auto 10px;
      height: 28px; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 18px;
      padding: 0 12px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.82);
      border: 2px solid var(--mac-black); box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 rgba(0,0,0,0.22);
      font-size: 13px;
    }
    .apple-dot {
      width: 16px; height: 16px; border: 2px solid var(--mac-black);
      border-radius: 50% 50% 45% 45%; background: var(--pink-hot);
      box-shadow: inset 3px 3px 0 rgba(255,255,255,0.55); flex: 0 0 auto;
    }
    .menu-item { white-space: nowrap; }
    .window {
      width: min(1200px, 100%); margin: 0 auto;
      border: 2px solid var(--mac-black); background: var(--mac-gray);
      box-shadow: 6px 6px 0 rgba(0,0,0,0.25);
      min-height: calc(100vh - 74px); display: flex; flex-direction: column;
    }
    .title-bar {
      min-height: 34px; display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 34px 1fr 84px;
      align-items: center; padding: 0 8px;
      background: repeating-linear-gradient(to bottom, var(--mac-gray-light) 0, var(--mac-gray-light) 2px, var(--mac-gray-mid) 3px, var(--mac-gray-mid) 4px);
      border-bottom: 2px solid var(--mac-black);
      font-size: 13px; font-weight: bold; text-align: center;
    }
    .close-box, .zoom-box {
      width: 18px; height: 18px; border: 2px solid var(--mac-black);
      background: var(--mac-white); display: grid; place-items: center;
      font-size: 12px; line-height: 1;
    }
    .zoom-box { justify-self: end; }
    .title-text {
      display: inline-block; justify-self: center; padding: 2px 12px;
      background: var(--mac-gray);
      border-left: 4px solid var(--mac-gray); border-right: 4px solid var(--mac-gray);
    }
    .toolbar {
      display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 10px;
      padding: 12px; background: var(--pink-soft);
      border-bottom: 2px solid var(--mac-black);
    }
    .tool-btn {
      width: 76px; min-height: 64px; border: 2px solid transparent;
      background: transparent; display: flex; flex-direction: column;
      align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 6px;
      font: inherit; font-size: 11px; cursor: pointer; color: var(--text);
    }
    .tool-btn:hover, .tool-btn.active {
      border-color: var(--mac-black); background: rgba(255,255,255,0.62);
      box-shadow: inset 2px 2px 0 rgba(0,0,0,0.12);
    }
    .tool-icon {
      width: 34px; height: 28px; border: 2px solid var(--mac-black);
      background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--mac-white) 0 35%, #ffd1e2 36% 100%);
      position: relative; border-radius: 2px;
    }
    .tool-icon::before {
      content: ""; position: absolute; top: -8px; left: 4px;
      width: 14px; height: 8px; border: 2px solid var(--mac-black);
      border-bottom: 0; background: #fff8fb;
    }
    .path-row {
      display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; padding: 8px 12px;
      background: var(--mac-gray-light); border-bottom: 2px solid var(--mac-black);
      font-size: 12px;
    }
    .path-label { white-space: nowrap; font-weight: bold; }
    .path-bar {
      flex: 1; min-width: 0; border: 2px solid var(--mac-black);
      background: var(--mac-white); padding: 5px 8px; height: 30px;
      display: flex; align-items: center; overflow: hidden;
      white-space: nowrap; text-overflow: ellipsis;
    }
    .go-btn {
      border: 2px solid var(--mac-black); background: var(--mac-white);
      padding: 4px 12px; height: 30px; font: inherit; cursor: pointer;
      box-shadow: 2px 2px 0 var(--mac-gray-dark);
    }
    .go-btn:active { transform: translate(1px,1px); box-shadow: 1px 1px 0 var(--mac-gray-dark); }
    .main {
      display: grid; grid-template-columns: 230px 1fr;
      gap: 0; flex: 1; min-height: 0; background: var(--mac-gray);
    }
    .sidebar { border-right: 2px solid var(--mac-black); padding: 12px; background: #f8d8e5; }
    .panel {
      border: 2px solid var(--mac-black); background: var(--pink-card);
      margin-bottom: 14px; padding: 10px;
      box-shadow: inset 2px 2px 0 rgba(255,255,255,0.8), inset -2px -2px 0 rgba(0,0,0,0.09);
    }
    .panel h3 {
      margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 12px; text-transform: lowercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.3px; border-bottom: 2px dotted var(--mac-black); padding-bottom: 5px;
    }
    .nav-list { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px; }
    .nav-link {
      display: block; padding: 6px 7px; color: var(--text);
      text-decoration: none; border: 2px solid transparent; font-size: 13px;
    }
    .nav-link:hover { background: var(--pink-hot); color: white; border-color: var(--mac-black); }
    .nav-link.active { background: #a8285f; color: white; border-color: var(--mac-black); }
    .content-wrap {
      padding: 12px; min-width: 0; display: flex;
      flex-direction: column; min-height: 0;
    }
    .browser-canvas {
      border: 2px solid var(--mac-black); background: #fffafd;
      flex: 1; min-height: 520px; padding: 26px; overflow: auto;
      box-shadow: inset 4px 4px 0 rgba(0,0,0,0.08);
    }
    .page { max-width: 830px; }
    .page-tag {
      display: inline-block; padding: 3px 8px; margin-bottom: 14px;
      border: 2px solid var(--mac-black); background: #ffe0ec;
      font-size: 12px; text-transform: lowercase;
    }
    h1 { margin: 0 0 14px; font-size: 34px; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: -1px; }
    h2 { margin: 24px 0 10px; font-size: 19px; font-weight: bold; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--mac-black); padding-bottom: 4px; }
    h3 { margin: 16px 0 6px; font-size: 15px; }
    p, li { line-height: 1.55; font-size: 14px; }
    p { margin: 0 0 12px; }
    ul { margin: 8px 0 14px 20px; padding: 0; }
    .placeholder-box, .resume-box {
      margin-top: 16px; padding: 16px;
      border: 2px dashed var(--mac-black); background: var(--pink-card);
    }
    .home-grid {
      display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(190px, 1fr));
      gap: 14px; margin-top: 20px;
    }
    .desktop-card {
      border: 2px solid var(--mac-black); padding: 16px; background: var(--mac-white);
      text-decoration: none; color: inherit; box-shadow: 4px 4px 0 rgba(216,79,139,0.25);
    }
    .desktop-card:hover { background: #ffe8f1; transform: translate(-1px,-1px); }
    .desktop-card-title { font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 7px; font-size: 14px; }
    .muted { color: #5a4a51; font-size: 13px; }
    .resume-header { border: 2px solid var(--mac-black); background: #ffe4ef; padding: 16px; margin-bottom: 16px; }
    .resume-contact { font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.6; }
    .resume-download {
      display: inline-block; margin: 6px 0 18px; padding: 8px 12px;
      border: 2px solid var(--mac-black); background: var(--mac-white);
      color: var(--text); text-decoration: none; box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 rgba(0,0,0,0.18);
    }
    .resume-download:hover { background: #ffe1ed; }
    .status-bar {
      min-height: 26px; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr auto auto;
      gap: 2px; padding: 3px; background: var(--mac-gray);
      border-top: 2px solid var(--mac-black); font-size: 12px;
    }
    .status-cell {
      border: 2px solid var(--mac-black); background: var(--mac-gray-light);
      padding: 3px 8px; display: flex; align-items: center; min-width: 0;
    }
    .status-right { min-width: 98px; justify-content: center; }

    .work-case {
      margin-top: 18px; padding: 18px;
      border: 2px solid var(--mac-black); background: var(--mac-white);
      box-shadow: 4px 4px 0 rgba(216,79,139,0.22);
    }
    .work-kicker {
      display: inline-block; padding: 3px 8px; margin-bottom: 8px;
      border: 2px solid var(--mac-black); background: #ffe0ec;
      font-size: 11px; text-transform: lowercase;
    }
    .work-meta {
      display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; margin: 10px 0 14px;
    }
    .meta-chip {
      border: 2px solid var(--mac-black); background: #fff4f8;
      padding: 4px 8px; font-size: 12px;
    }
    .work-image-grid {
      display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr));
      gap: 14px; margin: 16px 0 20px;
    }
    .work-image-card {
      margin: 0; padding: 10px; border: 2px solid var(--mac-black);
      background: #fffafd; cursor: zoom-in;
      box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 rgba(0,0,0,0.12);
    }
    .work-image-card:hover { box-shadow: 4px 5px 0 rgba(216,79,139,0.35); }
    .work-image-card img {
      width: 100%; display: block; border: 2px solid var(--mac-black);
      background: white;
    }
    .work-image-card figcaption {
      margin-top: 8px; font-size: 11px; line-height: 1.45;
      background: #ffe0ec; border: 2px solid var(--mac-black); padding: 6px 8px;
    }
    .reflection-card, .self-assessment {
      margin-top: 14px; padding: 14px;
      border: 2px solid var(--mac-black); background: var(--pink-card);
    }
    .self-assessment ul { margin-left: 18px; }
    @media (max-width: 820px) {
      body { padding: 8px; }
      .system-menu { gap: 10px; overflow-x: auto; }
      .main { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      .sidebar { border-right: 0; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--mac-black); }
      .browser-canvas { min-height: 420px; padding: 18px; }
      h1 { font-size: 27px; }
      .title-bar { grid-template-columns: 30px 1fr 42px; }
      .status-bar { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="system-menu" aria-label="classic mac menu bar">
    <div class="apple-dot" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <strong>finder</strong>
    <div class="menu-item">file</div>
    <div class="menu-item">edit</div>
    <div class="menu-item">view</div>
    <div class="menu-item">special</div>
    <div class="menu-item">help</div>
  </div>

  <div class="window">
    <div class="title-bar">
      <div class="close-box" aria-hidden="true">&times;</div>
      <div class="title-text">lauren cho portfolio</div>
      <div class="zoom-box" aria-hidden="true">&square;</div>
    </div>
    <div class="toolbar" id="toolbar"></div>
    <div class="path-row">
      <div class="path-label">location:</div>
      <div class="path-bar" id="addressBar">macintosh hd:portfolio:home</div>
      <button class="go-btn" id="homeBtn">home</button>
    </div>
    <div class="main">
      <aside class="sidebar">
        <div class="panel">
          <h3>folders</h3>
          <nav class="nav-list" id="sideNav"></nav>
        </div>
        <div class="panel">
          <h3>note</h3>
          <p class="muted">pink old mac-inspired portfolio shell for ui/ux, design work, case studies, and resume.</p>
        </div>
      </aside>
      <section class="content-wrap">
        <div class="browser-canvas" id="content"></div>
      </section>
    </div>
    <div class="status-bar">
      <div class="status-cell" id="statusText">ready</div>
      <div class="status-cell status-right">portfolio</div>
      <div class="status-cell status-right">classic mac</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div id="lb" style="display:none;position:fixed;inset:0;background:rgba(0,0,0,.88);z-index:9999;align-items:center;justify-content:center;cursor:zoom-out;" onclick="this.style.display='none'">
    <span style="position:fixed;top:18px;right:24px;color:#fff;font-size:36px;cursor:pointer;line-height:1;z-index:10000" onclick="document.getElementById('lb').style.display='none'">&times;</span>
    <img id="lb-img" src="" alt="enlarged screen" style="max-width:92vw;max-height:90vh;border:3px solid #fff;border-radius:8px;" />
  </div>

  <script>
    function openLB(src) {
      document.getElementById('lb-img').src = src;
      document.getElementById('lb').style.display = 'flex';
    }
    var before1 = "data:image/png;base64,";
    var before2 = "data:image/png;base64,";
    var before3 = "data:image/png;base64,";
    var before4 = "data:image/png;base64,";
    var before5 = "data:image/png;base64,";
    var before55 = "data:image/png;base64,";
    var before6 = "data:image/png;base64,";
    var after2 = "data:image/png;base64,";
    var after3 = "data:image/png;base64,";
    var after4 = "data:image/png;base64,";
    var after44 = "data:image/png;base64,";
    var caller = "data:image/png;base64,";
    var ba1 = "data:image/png;base64,";
    var ba2 = "data:image/png;base64,";


    var scaleSketch = "data:image/jpeg;base64,";
    var scaleFinal = "data:image/jpeg;base64,";

    var pages = {
      home: {
        title: "Home",
        path: "macintosh hd:portfolio:home",
        body: '<div class="page"><div class="page-tag">start page</div><h1>Lauren Cho</h1><p>i\'m a fourth-year uc san diego cognitive science student with a ui/ux focus, and i\'m interested in graphic design, web design, branding, and visual communication.</p><p>this portfolio is a pink old mac-inspired home for my projects, case studies, resume, and personal design work.</p><div class="home-grid"><a class="desktop-card" href="#works"><div class="desktop-card-title">works</div><div class="muted">selected ui/ux, graphic design, branding, and web projects.</div></a><a class="desktop-card" href="#case-study"><div class="desktop-card-title">case study</div><div class="muted">redesigning the iphone phone app for deaf &amp; hard-of-hearing users.</div></a><a class="desktop-card" href="#resume"><div class="desktop-card-title">resume</div><div class="muted">education, experience, skills, and a pdf download.</div></a><a class="desktop-card" href="#about"><div class="desktop-card-title">about me</div><div class="muted">my background, design interests, and contact info.</div></a></div></div>'
      },
      works: {
        title: "Works",
        path: "macintosh hd:portfolio:works",
        get body() {
          return `
            <div class="page">
              <div class="page-tag">selected work</div>
              <h1>Works</h1>
              <p>Selected UI/UX, interface, and visual design projects. This section shows both process and final work so the improvements are visible.</p>

              <article class="work-case">
                <div class="work-kicker">interface scale project</div>
                <h2>Inch / Foot / Yard Safety Scale</h2>
                <div class="work-meta">
                  <span class="meta-chip">tools: sketching, Figma</span>
                  <span class="meta-chip">focus: safety alerts</span>
                  <span class="meta-chip">scale: watch, phone, signage</span>
                </div>

                <p>My Inch/Foot/Yard scale was the first project where I was actively given critiques face to face. That kind of accountability made me want to be more conscious of how my designs present, as well as how they work.</p>

                <div class="work-image-grid">
                  <figure class="work-image-card" onclick="openLB('${scaleSketch}')">
                    <img src="${scaleSketch}" alt="Early handwritten sketch for the inch scale safety alert concept" />
                    <figcaption><strong>Before:</strong> initial sketch exploring glanceable Apple Watch alerts, color states, and haptic buzz counts.</figcaption>
                  </figure>
                  <figure class="work-image-card" onclick="openLB('${scaleFinal}')">
                    <img src="${scaleFinal}" alt="Final Inch Foot Yard safety scale interfaces" />
                    <figcaption><strong>After:</strong> final Inch / Foot / Yard system across watch alerts, phone route support, and exit signage.</figcaption>
                  </figure>
                </div>

                <h3>User goal</h3>
                <p>Here, I iterated several interfaces inspired by the Citizen and Waze apps. I tried to make the concept more practical by putting myself in the shoes of a user walking home alone at night. In that situation, split-second decisions are more useful than a process that takes the user through several different choices.</p>

                <h3>Design evolution</h3>
                <p>Besides wording and placement changes, the design I created was visually similar to my original sketch. The bigger change was in the system around it: the final version expands one watch idea into three scales of information. The inch scale gives immediate wrist feedback, the foot scale helps the user choose a safer route, and the yard scale makes exit-level guidance readable from farther away.</p>

                <h3>Rationale</h3>
                <p>I kept the red, yellow, and green alert levels because they let the user understand urgency without reading a long notification. I also kept haptic buzzes because the user may not be actively looking at their phone. The revisions focus on making the alert faster to understand, not just more visually polished.</p>

                <div class="self-assessment">
                  <h3>Self assessment</h3>
                  <ul>
                    <li><strong>What I learned:</strong> Critique made me notice that presentation changes whether people trust and understand a design.</li>
                    <li><strong>What improved:</strong> The project moved from one rough watch concept into a clearer multi-scale safety system with before-and-after development.</li>
                    <li><strong>What I would revise next:</strong> I would test the wording and buzz patterns with people walking so I could see whether the alerts are actually understandable under stress.</li>
                  </ul>
                </div>
              </article>
            </div>
          `;
        }
      },
      resume: {
        title: "Resume",
        path: "macintosh hd:portfolio:resume",
        body: '<div class="page"><div class="page-tag">document</div><div class="resume-header"><h1>Lauren Cho</h1><div class="resume-contact">San Diego, CA &middot; 213-507-7734 &middot; lscho@ucsd.edu</div></div><a class="resume-download" href="LaurenChoResume2026.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">open resume pdf</a><h2>summary</h2><p>Fourth-year UC San Diego Cognitive Science student with a UI/UX focus and experience in graphic design, web design, branding, event support, and customer-facing roles. Skilled in Figma, Adobe Creative Cloud, logo design, and visual communication. Fluent in English and conversationally fluent in Korean.</p><h2>education</h2><div class="resume-box"><h3>University of California, San Diego</h3><p>B.S. Cognitive Science, UI/UX Focus<br>Fourth-Year Undergraduate &middot; June 2026</p></div><h2>experience</h2><div class="resume-box"><h3>Graphic Designer | TREND, UC San Diego | 2024&ndash;2025</h3><ul><li>Designed graphics and visual assets for student-facing content while supporting cohesive branding and layout consistency.</li><li>Collaborated on publication and promotional materials that communicated clearly to campus audiences.</li></ul><h3>Booth Staff / Brand Experience Support | Hoyoverse Booth, San Diego Comic-Con | 2024</h3><ul><li>Supported attendee interaction, crowd flow, and front-facing booth operations in a high-traffic convention setting.</li><li>Represented the brand while helping deliver a positive visitor experience during San Diego Comic-Con.</li></ul></div><h2>skills</h2><div class="resume-box"><p><strong>design:</strong> graphic design, web design, logo design, visual branding, layout design, UI/UX design</p><p><strong>tools:</strong> Figma, Adobe Creative Cloud, Photoshop, Illustrator, InDesign, XD, Acrobat, After Effects, Premiere Pro</p><p><strong>languages:</strong> English (fluent), Korean (conversational fluency)</p></div></div>'
      },
      about: {
        title: "About Me",
        path: "macintosh hd:portfolio:about",
        body: '<div class="page"><div class="page-tag">profile</div><h1>About Me</h1><p>i\'m lauren, a uc san diego cognitive science student focused on ui/ux. i like making interfaces feel expressive, clear, and visually memorable.</p><p>my background includes graphic design, web design, logo design, figma, adobe creative cloud, and front-facing brand experience work.</p><div class="placeholder-box"><p>i will add a longer personal bio, portrait, and social/contact links here later.</p></div></div>'
      },
      contact: {
        title: "Contact",
        path: "macintosh hd:portfolio:contact",
        body: '<div class="page"><div class="page-tag">info</div><h1>Contact</h1><p>email: lscho@ucsd.edu</p><p>portfolio: excalibrr.github.io/laurenchoportfolio/</p><div class="placeholder-box"><p>i can add github, linkedin, instagram, or any other links here.</p></div></div>'
      }
    };

    pages["case-study"] = {
      title: "Case Study",
      path: "macintosh hd:portfolio:case-study",
      get body() {
        return `
          <style>
            .flow-strip { display:flex; gap:10px; overflow-x:auto; padding-bottom:12px; margin:14px 0 20px; scrollbar-width:thin; scrollbar-color:#d84f8b #ffe7f0; }
            .flow-frame { flex:0 0 auto; width:150px; border:2px solid #111; background:#fff; cursor:zoom-in; box-shadow:3px 3px 0 rgba(216,79,139,.3); transition:transform .15s; }
            .flow-frame:hover { transform:translateY(-3px); box-shadow:4px 6px 0 rgba(216,79,139,.45); }
            .flow-frame img { width:100%; display:block; border-bottom:2px solid #111; }
            .flow-frame .frame-label { font-size:10px; padding:4px 6px; background:#ffe0ec; text-align:center; line-height:1.4; }
            .ba-img-block { margin:14px 0 20px; border:2px solid #111; background:#fff; box-shadow:4px 4px 0 rgba(0,0,0,.15); cursor:zoom-in; }
            .ba-img-block:hover { box-shadow:5px 5px 0 rgba(216,79,139,.4); }
            .ba-img-block img { width:100%; display:block; }
            .ba-img-label { font-size:11px; font-weight:bold; padding:6px 10px; background:#ffe0ec; border-top:2px solid #111; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:.5px; }
            .caller-block { display:flex; gap:16px; align-items:flex-start; margin:14px 0 20px; }
            .caller-img { width:180px; flex-shrink:0; border:2px solid #111; box-shadow:3px 3px 0 rgba(216,79,139,.3); cursor:zoom-in; }
            .caller-img img { width:100%; display:block; }
            .caller-img:hover { box-shadow:4px 5px 0 rgba(216,79,139,.5); }
            .cs-divider { border:none; border-top:2px dashed #d84f8b; margin:22px 0; }
            @media(max-width:620px){ .caller-block { flex-direction:column; } .caller-img { width:100%; } .flow-frame { width:120px; } }
          </style>
          <div class="page">
            <div class="page-tag">case study &middot; cogs 127</div>
            <h1>Redesigning the iPhone Phone App for Deaf &amp; Hard-of-Hearing Users</h1>
            <p>A phone&rsquo;s most fundamental feature is making phone calls. We asked a simple question: does this basic experience actually work for everyone? <strong>It doesn&rsquo;t.</strong></p>
            <p>Around 48 million Americans have some degree of hearing loss. Our team redesigned the iOS Phone app to support deaf and hard-of-hearing users through the full arc of a call &mdash; preparation, IVR navigation, live captions, type-to-speech, and post-call summaries. These tools belong natively in the same action sheet as Call Recording, not hidden in Settings.</p>

            <hr class="cs-divider" />
            <h2>What Brought Us Here</h2>
            <p>We kept returning to one fundamental question: what happens when the most basic app on your phone &mdash; the Phone app &mdash; doesn&rsquo;t work for you? Phones were designed around voice. Keyboards were designed around sight. We wanted to design for the people who fall through both gaps.</p>
            <p>Apple has made progress, including Live Captions introduced in iOS 16 and expanded in iOS 26. But the people who need phone accessibility most often don&rsquo;t know it exists. Our project proposes making accessibility a first-class citizen of the call UI, not an afterthought in a settings menu.</p>

            <hr class="cs-divider" />
            <h2>User Research</h2>
            <p>I went in with assumptions. I assumed deaf users wanted technology that helps them function more like hearing people &mdash; that the goal was to close a gap. Our interviews entirely changed that framing.</p>
            <p>One participant, Selena, is a CODA (Child of Deaf Adults) and co-president of UCSD&rsquo;s ASL club. She corrected my assumption that Deaf people are eager to assimilate into hearing culture. She also shared something that shaped our design significantly: &ldquo;Even through an interpreter feels better than just typing to each other.&rdquo; ASL is a visual-spatial language with grammar, emotion, and nuance that English text can&rsquo;t capture. Captions are functional &mdash; but not preferred. This pushed us to include sign-to-speech (using the front camera to recognize ASL) as a future-state feature.</p>

